Test suite keiro-test: RUNNING...

Keiro.Workflow.Inspection
  opaque cursors
    round-trips Unicode and exact timestamps, rejects foreign kinds and oversized tokens [✔]
  rechecks every header field against its exact image, including old and far-future dates [✔]
  rejects header images before returning oversized text or escaped JSON [✔]
  reads fresh, owner-scoped headers through a reused session action [✔]
  rejects an outgoing cursor that clients could not resume within the cursor limit [✔]
  preserves large ordinary keys and includes them in both list orderings [✔]
  pages wide keys without an obsolete exceptional-population limit [✔]
  orders by id before name and refuses the old key cursor kind [✔]
  classifies every stored row identically in Haskell and SQL without modifying rows [✔]
  pages key order completely, and omits continuation on a full final page [✔]
  pages newest creation first including tied timestamps and observes an empty page clock [✔]
  rejects sizes and malformed or cross-order cursors before reading [✔]
  applies half-open creation and update windows [✔]
  observes then-current inserts strictly beyond the cursor [✔]
  independently pages journal and steps and rejects cross-owner and rotated generation cursors [✔]
  pages children and directly allocated awakeables through their owning tables [✔]
  raises the runtime's decode error instead of returning a partial corrupt journal [✔]
Keiro.Projection.Catalog
  derives typed live handlers, registrations, inventory, and one stable fingerprint [✔]
  resolves several query models to one multi-target owner without list-order dependence [✔]
  derives cursor authority from the owner and validates waiting scope [✔]
  fingerprints freshness and cursor policy only in the owning group slice [✔]
  rejects empty and split-owner query target sets with stable derived diagnostics [✔]
  keeps supply derived from canonical owner and observed-target facts [✔]
  fingerprints and renders checkpoint policy without changing subscription identity [✔]
  reports missing and independent duplicate owners with every claim site [✔]
  accumulates stable identity and reference diagnostics independent of input order [✔]
  rejects duplicate physical tables and runtime registry names [✔]
  rejects cross-group writes, dependency cycles, and unsafe replay combinations [✔]
  accepts every explicit policy except current-head seeding after a replayable clear [✔]
  rejects all-stream/category overlap while accepting distinct category fan-in [✔]
